{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers","id":979809,"title":"Real Life 'Superpowers'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T12:55:15-07:00","id":979809,"title":"Real Life 'Superpowers'","content":"One thing that the vast majority of RPGs do not accurately reflect are real life 'superpowers' (positive adaptations or mutations that allow humans to exceed normal human performance without exacting a proportional cost). For example, there are people whose bones densities are eight times greater (not eight percent, but eight times greater) than that of normal times beings (<a href=\"http://www.the-scientist.com/?articles.view/articleNo/24344/title/The-world-s-densest-bones/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.the-scientist.com/?articl...densest-bones/</a>). They have problems swimming because their bone density is so high, but they cannot break bones under normal circumstances (any force that could break their bones would liquefy their soft tissue long before it broke their bones). Other, less impressive though useful abilities include underwater vision, immunity to specific diseases, and the ability to tolerate low oxygen environments, none of which can be properly accounted for in WoD (or in the 'realistic' campaigns of more universal gaming systems). So, the question is, how do you reflect real life 'superpowers' in a gaming system like WoD, where you have superpowered entities running around, without breaking the system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:50:19-07:00","id":979991,"title":"","content":"(AT, your example is also covered in a more technical form <a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1359/JBMR.041223/full\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.)<br /> <br /> They stick Iron Stomach in CofD over and over again, yet so much else goes unaccounted for...<br /> <br /> Thrombophilia, an increased tendency toward clotting aka the opposite of hemophilia, has likely lasted for as long as it has on account of how good it is to not bleed out from being attacked by wild predators, whatever other complications might follow. Unfortunately, individuals with disorders such as Hughes Syndrome (autoimmune-triggered thrombophilia) are also at a greater risk of deep vein clots and strokes if they don't move around enough, which is the pits for modern living unless you happen to live in a foot-friendly city. Scabs on people such as myself will also look odd, like some kind of lighter-shaded crystalline surface on the skin.<br /> <br /> While it is, of course, unlisted in the WoD, it would seem to form a natural complement to the Hemophiliac flaw in Hunter's Hunted 2. Somehow. There don't seem to be very substantial bleeding rules anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:01:23-07:00","id":980047,"title":"","content":"Strange that they consider it a disorder. Evolution would reward high bone density or enhanced clotting factors though, of course, it is not that beneficial in modern society. I guess it depends on context, and a critical evolutionary advantage 1000 years ago is a quirk of genetics nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:34:27-07:00","id":980068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=980047#post980047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that they consider it a disorder. Evolution would reward high bone density or enhanced clotting factors though, of course, it is not that beneficial in modern society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the hyperostis causes some troublesome growths to pop up in the hard palates of people with it (catching food particles and causing constant infections), as noted in the article, while Hughes Syndrome causes frequent miscarriages. So yes, there is cause to label it a disorder; no one wants to deal with those things personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess it depends on context, and a critical evolutionary advantage 1000 years ago is a quirk of genetics nowadays. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call either a ritical advantage; they seem to be very rare, with no widespread propagation in sight. In the lab of the wide-open wilderness, they're moderate local successes, with hyperdense bones likely requiring way more calcium in the diet and thus a more frequent need to go out and find food. Also, selection pressures have always been context specific; being able to metabolize oxygen wasn't so great until cyanobacteria started pumping it out in sufficient volume to drive most of the obligate anaerobes into soil layers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:19:07-07:00","id":980099,"title":"","content":"If it was a critical evolutionary advantage, everyone would have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T01:23:26-07:00","id":980155,"title":"","content":"These advantages/disorders are nothing other than etherites/technomancers trying to bring their stuff into the consensus.<br /> <br /> IMO at least...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:59:49-07:00","id":980239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=980155#post980155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These advantages/disorders are nothing other than etherites/technomancers trying to bring their stuff into the consensus.<br /> <br /> IMO at least...</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GzQ564jop8\" data-code=\"3GzQ564jop8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3GzQ564jop8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:13:41-07:00","id":982104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers#post979809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that the vast majority of RPGs do not accurately reflect are real life 'superpowers' (positive adaptations or mutations that allow humans to exceed normal human performance without exacting a proportional cost). For example, there are people whose bones densities are eight times greater (not eight percent, but eight times greater) than that of normal times beings (<a href=\"http://www.the-scientist.com/?articles.view/articleNo/24344/title/The-world-s-densest-bones/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.the-scientist.com/?articl...densest-bones/</a>). They have problems swimming because their bone density is so high, but they cannot break bones under normal circumstances (any force that could break their bones would liquefy their soft tissue long before it broke their bones). Other, less impressive though useful abilities include underwater vision, immunity to specific diseases, and the ability to tolerate low oxygen environments, none of which can be properly accounted for in WoD (or in the 'realistic' campaigns of more universal gaming systems). So, the question is, how do you reflect real life 'superpowers' in a gaming system like WoD, where you have superpowered entities running around, without breaking the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a friend of mine has an overdeveloped sense of smell, at the point he can &quot;sense&quot; if someone did drink from his beer while he was in another room (and sometime he can even discern if the culprit is male or female), but obvioulsy he has lots of problems because most smells are &quot;bad smells&quot; for him (and frankly I find him rather annoying).<br /> Another friend of mine has a really good &quot;ear&quot;, he can discern sounds that no one around can, but on the other side his limit of auditory pain (the limit above which a loud sound become painful or damage the eardrum) is much lower than others, and he has problem discerning whispered words because there are always background noises he can detect and &quot;normal&quot; people can't.<br /> <br /> These are two inconveniencing &quot;superpowers&quot; -the Auspex (1) most used applications along with 20/10 sight- that become troubling in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 10-05-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:03:13-07:00","id":982211,"title":"","content":"I've never found 20/10 sight to be troubling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:05:55-07:00","id":982727,"title":"","content":"badly written, &quot;20/10 sight&quot; was related to &quot;Auspex (1) most used applications&quot;, not &quot;become troubling in real life.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:43:49-07:00","id":982822,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay. Thank you for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:59:48-07:00","id":983325,"title":"","content":"* For game mechanic effects they can be merits.<br /> <br /> * Human echolocalitation. There are cases with names and surnames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:28:56-07:00","id":983337,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the system itself does not include them, so it is difficult to determine the proper cost for game balance purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:18:04-07:00","id":983358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=983337#post983337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the system itself does not include them, so it is difficult to determine the proper cost for game balance purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fine, since most abnormalities would not confer any significant advantage in-game. It is unnecessary to make a specific merit about having a slightly keener sense of smell, or a flaw that involves having small, benign lesions on the roof of your mouth. Shit's just irrelevant...<br /> <br /> If you really, really want to portray this stuff for whatever reason, you could probably just use it to justify attribute choices: 'my blood clots a little bit faster than normal, so I have relatively high stamina.' Actually coming up with harder rules for such a minute advantage would be inappropriate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-07-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:35:17-07:00","id":983399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=983358#post983358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is fine, since most abnormalities would not confer any significant advantage in-game. It is unnecessary to make a specific merit about having a slightly keener sense of smell, or a flaw that involves having small, benign lesions on the roof of your mouth. Shit's just irrelevant...<br /> <br /> If you really, really want to portray this stuff for whatever reason, you could probably just use it to justify attribute choices: 'my blood clots a little bit faster than normal, so I have relatively high stamina.' Actually coming up with harder rules for such a minute advantage would be inappropriate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Clotting faster probably wouldn't do that, but I have yet to see bleeding rules in this branch of the system like they are in Exalted, so who knows what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:40:44-07:00","id":983433,"title":"","content":"If one of my players would ask me, if he can take one of these, I would answer: \u201cSure, let me see... this is extremely rare, right? So it will be 5 Freebies for your Superpower, and I write the mechanics. Still interested?\u201c<br /> In a mage game it could be just the coincidental explanation for your effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:58:35-07:00","id":983477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=983399#post983399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clotting faster probably wouldn't do that, but I have yet to see bleeding rules in this branch of the system like they are in Exalted, so who knows what.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is WoD generally has a more macro-level scope to the rules. A one in a million syndrome that make your limbs a bit more flexible or your sweat stickier generally doesn't need their own system. If you made this a central focal point to your game so that you need these things statted out, I think you only need to come up with the rules for a single flaw: myopia.<br /> <br /> It is a little odd that vampire, a game obsessed with blood, does not have a general rule of thumb for bleeding out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:46:09-07:00","id":983645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=983477#post983477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is WoD generally has a more macro-level scope to the rules. A one in a million syndrome that make your limbs a bit more flexible or your sweat stickier generally doesn't need their own system. If you made this a central focal point to your game so that you need these things statted out, I think you only need to come up with the rules for a single flaw: myopia.<br /> <br /> It is a little odd that vampire, a game obsessed with blood, does not have a general rule of thumb for bleeding out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:29:55-07:00","id":983663,"title":"","content":"I have always made mortal players check for bleeding if they take more health levels than their Stamina in damage. The roll is Stamina (difficulty 6 plus every health level of damage in excess of their Stamina). If they fail, they take one health level of damage, on the type that triggered the bleeding roll, and get to check for continued bleeding the next turn, at the same difficulty. If they botch, they temporarily lose one dot of Stamina, which only heals when they heal the damage. If it reduces them to '0' Stamina, they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:48:25-07:00","id":983671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/979809-real-life-superpowers?p=983663#post983663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always made mortal players check for bleeding if they take more health levels than their Stamina in damage. The roll is Stamina (difficulty 6 plus every health level of damage in excess of their Stamina). If they fail, they take one health level of damage, on the type that triggered the bleeding roll, and get to check for continued bleeding the next turn, at the same difficulty. If they botch, they temporarily lose one dot of Stamina, which only heals when they heal the damage. If it reduces them to '0' Stamina, they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has some major probability problems, since botches are going to be extremely common with the difficulty hike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}